From f7d8af70bec960f9acd62c123b969f4c3b613f6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:20:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sim): crossing law reads a shared vertex a rounding apart
 as a touch

The verifier's crossing law (a) tested orientation signs exactly, so two
moves meeting at one vertex reached twice, a rounding apart, could read
as a proper crossing and hold the post. A chord end within
CROSSING_TOUCH (1e-9 mm, a point-to-point distance) of one of the other
chord's END points now reads as on its line, as an exact shared vertex
always did. Only end points are excused, not the whole line, so a walk
passing through a chord at a vertex a picometre off its interior still
reports (the #1134 review's probe). proper_cross itself is unchanged for
dist2_segs and the arc-wall law.

Fixes #1129

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
